# Go Hooks

> This file extends the common hooks rule with Go specific content.

## PostToolUse Behavior

After any edit to a `.go` file, run these checks in order. Surface all output and stop until each step succeeds.

1. `gofmt -w` — mandatory formatting
2. `goimports -w` — group and prune imports
3. `golangci-lint run --fix` — supersedes `go vet` and `staticcheck`; catches errcheck, ineffassign, unused, revive. Do not run vet or staticcheck separately.
4. `go test ./... -race` — required because `pkg/registry/` uses concurrent fetches. Catch races at edit time.

Do not run `go build`. The language server already catches compile errors.

### Wire to agent runtime

- Claude Code → `~/.claude/settings.json` (PostToolUse)
- Cursor → `.cursor/hooks/` (project-local)
- Other → agent-specific configuration
